    "description": "Track a task through the idea-to-ship flow",
    "argumentHint": "[new [<what are we doing>] | board | switch <slug> | use <workflow> | doc [pointer] | bar | share <link> | jev [off|shadow|on] | settings | recap [new] | why | skip | followup | approve | allow | done]"
   }
  ],
  "tools": [
   {
    "name": "stage_done",
    "description": "Call this once when the work of the current flow stage is finished (not after each question), with a one-line summary of what was done. The flow mod records it and answers with the task's next step. A build stage is recorded only once its checks pass. Call it with outcome 'blocked' when you cannot finish without the person."
   },
   {
    "name": "ask_jev",
    "description": "Ask Jev, TypeSafe's small judgment model, yes/no or pick-one questions about facts you pass in. Use it only when the person asked for Jev, or to settle a judgment call while grilling or planning. Put every fact the questions need in `state`: Jev judges those facts, not your framing, and sees nothing else. Each answer comes back with its probability and settled (true at 0.75 or more). Re-ask the unsettled ones with sharper facts, and stop when all are settled or a round adds nothing. Jev's answer is advice for you. It is never the person's approval of a gate, a spec or tickets."
   }
  ],
